# rpg/art/doll/clips/actions/common.clip: the body actions every fighter shares (ACTIONS-BODY, P2c wave 2; STYLE_P2 25.8
# items 8-10; contracts 5). GENERATED by the area's src/clips.py. Format: rpg/art/doll/doll.h.
# ROLL (4 x 85 ms, the sim's 0.34 s): crouch (bob 5, the upper body leaning into the roll, the fists low, the weapon
# trailing); tuck (composed in the left view curled tight, bob 9, the head bowed, laid down a quarter toward the roll:
# turn=east facing R); over (the other quarter); rise (the buckle legs, bob 3, the fists at the waist). Round 4 (B10 on
# the T5 forge spearman): both turned frames sit 2 px up, so every facing has the same east and west
# atlas cuts; the back view (U) lands in its crouch (its fourth frame is the first: one cut).
# Every garment, armour, helm and cloak turns with the body (contracts 5), so nothing needs a roll view.
# CAST (gather while the spell is held, then release): gather (weight back, the fists together at the chest with the
# glow over them, under the chin, eyes narrowed), release (weight forward, both arms thrust toward the aim).
# Every frame keeps the held weapon in the right fist (both fists on its line: C3d holds for the hafts).
# HURT with gear: the shipped flinch with the head (and so the helm) snapped back a pixel for `capped` looks; a capped
# shield bearer also drops the shield arm a pixel facing D / U (these lines come before shield.clip's, so they win).
# (wave-2 fix round, ACTIONS r1, PLAN D81: no weapon pixel more than 2 rows below the sole row) an archer rolls with the
# bow slung on the back (held=- bowback=rest, as in the LOCO frames): held low in the crouch and the rise it ran 3-8 rows
# under the soles facing D / U; the longbow's cast facing D / U holds it at the nock (bw_nock, held=nock), a row higher.
# (wave-2 fix round 2, ACTIONS; PLAN D81: the off fist on every ACTION frame of a two-handed weapon) a two-handed weapon
# rolls with its haft along the tumbling body (`when twohand`: the tuck and the over at weapon=292.5): at 270 it lay flat
# across the curled body like a bar and both fists missed its line by 2 px (C3d: the greatsword, the spear, the glaive).
# (wave-2 fix round 4, ACTIONS; C3d 32) the cast release facing U with a weapon in hand: a one-handed weapon rides the
# guard fist out at the side (oh_g, the drawn idle's arm: the whole fist clear of a cape; it sat a pixel past the cape's
# edge, the grip under it), the off hand releasing; a two-handed weapon stays in both fists at the chest (csgather, hidden
# by the back, both fists on the haft: D90) and swings up behind the right shoulder (a045). The signed-off hero lines
# (`herokit`) keep their cast (PLAN D94).

